    "id": 10378,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "You can cancel a chase dash with a guard. In getting close to your opponent with a chase dash, you may be hit by their attacks. Avoid this by canceling the chase dash with a guard and see what they do next.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0020:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10399,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Evading Attacks",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0020:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10379,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Use sidesteps and backsteps to evade your opponent's tracking and dodge attacks.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0020:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10379,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "When doing a Quick Step, your skill gauge will momentarily stop recovering. Excessively doing a Quick Step will stop the skill gauge from recovering completely, so time your evades wisely.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0030:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10400,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Quick Dodge",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0030:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10380,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "You can interrupt light attacks, aerial attacks, and certain skills like demon skills with a Quick Dodge (Quick Step, jump, and chase dash).",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0030:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10380,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Even though Quick Dodge consumes a portion of your skill gauge upon activation, it can eliminate any openings that your opponent can take advantage of. Master this skill to reduce the risk of getting hit by attacks.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0030:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10380,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "By memorizing actions that can be canceled with Quick Dodge, you'll have an advantage in battle. Be sure to check the character command list as well.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0040:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10401,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Shove",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0040:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10381,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Use shove to put space between yourself and your opponent's attacks. In addition to avoiding being excessively hit, using shove will let you move faster than if you had guarded against your opponent's attack.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0040:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10381,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Furthermore, you can use shove to act quickly and release unblockable skills and attacks to counter your opponent.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0040:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10381,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "Keep in mind that using shove can be ineffective against some attacks like throws and heavy attacks.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0050:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10402,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Boost and Surge",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0050:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10382,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "When using Boost or Surge, your skill gauge, support gauge, and demon gauge will refill. If playing as a demon, your HP will also be restored.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0050:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10382,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "A refilled support gauge and demon gauge will up your survival rate since both gauges are needed for an emergency escape.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0050:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10382,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "As you get used to fighting, you'll use Boost and Surge to refill your support gauge and demon gauge more often. With practice, you'll learn the best time to activate them.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0060:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10403,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Guard Break",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0060:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10383,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "When using a guard against your opponent's attacks, your guard strength will reduce, which could result in a guard break. If this happens, you'll be defenseless.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0060:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10383,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "To greatly reduce your opponent's guard strength, make use of the chase dash. Also, if you land a fully charged heavy attack, you'll immediately trigger a guard break.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0070:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10404,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Beginner Battle Tips: Aerial Attacks (Plunge)",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0070:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10384,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "While most characters have this feature, check the command list to confirm that the character you are controlling has this ability.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0080:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10405,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Defense",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0080:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10385,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Because each character has different levels of defense, they each take different degrees of damage. Characters with lower levels of defense will take more damage.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0080:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10385,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Practice with each character to see their level of defense.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0090:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10406,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Parry",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0090:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10386,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Counter your opponent's incoming attacks with a parry. If your parry succeeds, you'll be able to hurt your opponent. If it fails, you risk receiving a counterattack from your opponent.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0090:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10386,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Of course, it is difficult to land a parry since your opponent will be wary of them. Pay attention to attacks with timing that cannot be changed. (For example: skills that are not affected by Quick Dodge or support skills that cannot be interrupted.)",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0090:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10386,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "The timing of support skills is completely fixed once activated. Watch these types of attacks carefully and time your parry. Once you've mastered this, you'll become a fearsome opponent.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0100:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10407,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Heavy Attacks",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0100:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10387,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Heavy attacks require charging up in addition to attacking your opponent. As such, these attacks continuously consume a small portion of your skill gauge. In other words, if the amount built up in your skill gauge is insufficient, charging and attacking will be limited.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0100:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10387,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Make sure you have enough of your skill gauge filled to pull off a heavy attack. The skill gauge is only consumed during the charge up and release of a heavy attack, so you're free to unleash other attacks near your opponent that don't require a charge.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0110:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10408,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Throw Strategies",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0110:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10388,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Jumping is effective against throws. Avoid throws by jumping when your opponent attempts to grab you.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0110:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10388,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "If it is difficult to time your jump just right, try activating Boost when you think your opponent will grab you. If your opponent actually does try to grab you, you'll send them flying by activating Boost.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0120:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10409,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Tracking Attacks",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0120:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10389,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Some attacks cannot be evaded with a Quick Step. These tracking attacks nullify evasion because the character is locked on the target and will dash to hit them.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0120:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10389,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Check the character's command list to see which attacks nullify evasion. Knowing the characteristics of attacks will improve your odds of winning.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0130:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10410,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: When the Skill Gauge Refills",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0130:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10390,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Although the skill gauge automatically refills after use, the time it starts to refill depends on the type of skill that was used.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0130:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10390,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "The skill gauge may start refilling right away or be delayed. (The more the skill gauge is used, the more time it will take for the gauge to start refilling.)",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0130:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10390,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "By knowing the ins and outs of your attacks and their influence on the skill gauge refilling, you can eliminate the risk of running out of your skill gauge when you need to use it. Try to keep this in mind as you play.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0140:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10411,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Intermediate Battle Tips: Special Gauge",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0140:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10391,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "The special gauge fills as you attack and perform all types of actions. Even using a chase dash will fill the special gauge. Small actions and attacks like light and aerial attacks will fill the special gauge slightly. On the other hand, skills will fill the special gauge more.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0140:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10391,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "The special gauge will easily refill when you are proactive in attacking, so keep this in mind during battle.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0140:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10391,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "In addition to this, the light attack 4-hit combo (lower) will refill the special gauge by a considerable amount. While the combo does eventually end, this is the best way to build up the special gauge if you need it.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0150:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10412,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Combo Pointers 1",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0150:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10392,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "As you perform a combo, the damage inflicted with each successive hit in the combo decreases. This is due to a damage scaling system, which has a degree of reduction predetermined for each attack.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0150:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10392,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "This damage scaling varies by attack, so try out different combos during Practice Mode to see which ones inflict the most overall damage.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0160:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10413,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Combo Pointers 2",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0160:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10393,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "When doing a combo, the overall damage inflicted may change depending on the first attack that lead the combo.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0160:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10393,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "For example, when initiating a combo with a rush-type attack like a chase dash, the damage inflicted is reduced. (Initiating a combo with attacks that are easier to land will tend to have reduced damage.)",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0160:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10393,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "On the other hand, some combos increase the overall damage inflicted if the attack is difficult to land. You can see the differences for yourself in Practice Mode.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0170:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10414,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Features of Heavy Attacks 1",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0170:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10394,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Heavy attacks function differently, depending on whether or not they are fully charged. If you are hit by your opponent during pursuit, you will not flinch. However, this feature wears off right before you attack, so keep this in mind.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0170:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10394,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "Because you can use a Quick Dodge when your heavy attack is not fully charged, even if your opponent evades your attack, you can pursue them with a chase dash through a Quick Dodge. Being able to think on your feet can be a good offensive strategy.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0170:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10394,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "Also, because you do not flinch until right before an attack, if you time it right with your opponent's attack, you have the chance for a yellow combo timer to appear. Since it's possible to get a combo this way, it's definitely worth attempting.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0180:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10415,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Features of Heavy Attacks 2",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0180:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10395,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "If your heavy attack is fully charged, you will not flinch during the attack. Since this can be used as a means of winning against an opponent, use it to deliver the final blow.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0180:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10395,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "However, when your heavy attack is fully charged, it'll be impossible to Quick Dodge out of it. So if your opponent evades the attack, there will be a large opening that they could take advantage of. It is best to use this fully charged feature during close combat, where it would be difficult for your opponent to evade your heavy attack.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0180:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10395,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "Also, a fully charged heavy attack will land and nullify your opponent's recovery state. Use this to turn the tides of battle and go on the offensive.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0190:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10416,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Guard Strength Recovery",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0190:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10396,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "A short while after using guard against an opponent's attack, your guard strength will recover.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0190:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10396,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "If you try to guard as your guard strength is recovering, the recovery rate will slow down while the guard is held in place. If the shove action is performed, your guard strength will stop recovering completely.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0190:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10396,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "Overusing guard increases the risk of a guard break. Have a move ready to go to avoid overusing your guard.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Title_0200:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10417,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "Advanced Battle Tips: Quick Dodge Techniques",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0200:11" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10397,
    "idSub": 11,
    "message": "When a player uses a skill corresponding to a Quick Dodge and follows it up with a chase dash, the player must use their skill gauge to activate the chase dash. However, keep in mind that you can use other skills to follow up with that don't consume the skill gauge.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0200:21" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10397,
    "idSub": 21,
    "message": "This will depend on the timing of the chase dash after a skill is used. In other words, a chase dash can occur within the timing of a skill finishing, counting it as part of the skill itself. If you wait until after a skill lands and the movement is completely over, it will be possible to do a chase dash without using up your skill gauge.",
  },
  "Tutorial_Battle_Message_0200:31" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10397,
    "idSub": 31,
    "message": "When using skills with this mechanic in mind, you can perform combos that use less of your overall skill gauge. Try to learn this mechanic by studying the skills and combos in Practice Mode and other places.",
  },
  "Tutorial_NoReplace_Message_0010:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
