    "message": "Parrying",
  },
  "Tutorial_title_0075_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10655,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Reward Mission Progress",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0023_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10485,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "At the top of the screen is a set of two gauges. The green bar is the health gauge (also known as HP), and the blue bar is the skill gauge.

If you reduce your opponent's health gauge to zero, you win! But watch out—if your own health gauge reaches zero, you lose.

Your skill gauge depletes as you use your skills, but it replenishes itself naturally over time.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0023_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10486,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "At the bottom of the screen is the special gauge, which will fill as you hit or get hit by an opponent.

Once you fill an entire bar, the number to the side of the gauge will increase. You can stock up to three bars in this way.

Consume special bars to Boost your strength or unleash your Ultimate Art.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0023_02:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10487,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "The circular timer next to the combo counter indicates how long you can continue your combo, and the length is determined by the attack used to start the combo.

Green Timer: Long
Yellow Timer: Medium
Red Timer: Short

Try to pull off a powerful combo before time runs out. If you hit the opponent just after the timer runs out they will be blown away, forcibly ending the combo.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0024_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10488,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In battles where the opponent has a gauge above their head, you may see the opening thread after either parrying an aura attack (quickly tilt <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/> and simultaneously press <kcId_kcId_Battle_Guard/>) or bringing the opponent to low health.

When you see the opening thread, press <kcId_kcId_Battle_SUKINOITO/> to finish them off in a single strike.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0027_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10489,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Some battles allow an ally to join you as a support fighter.

The yellow bar is the support gauge. By pressing <kcId_kcId_Battle_Support/> when at least half of this gauge is full, you can call on your ally to assist you in various ways.

Once spent, the support gauge will continue to replenish itself over time.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0027_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10490,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Support fighters can be called upon for three different actions.

Support Skill:
Press <kcId_kcId_Battle_Support/> to summon your ally to attack the opponent. Consumes 50% of the support gauge.

Emergency Escape:
Press <kcId_kcId_Battle_Support/> the moment you get hit by an attack to have your ally carry you to safety. Consumes 100% of the support gauge.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0027_02:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10491,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Switch:
Hold <kcId_kcId_Battle_Support/> to switch out with your ally. However, note that all gauges are shared between both fighters. Consumes 50% of the support gauge.

Switching out will not replenish the health gauge.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0029_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10492,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If you come in contact with poison from an opponent or a puddle on the ground, you will be afflicted with the poison, causing your health to gradually deplete. The poison status will cure itself in time, but it's best to avoid it from the start.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0030_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10493,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If your fighter's health reaches zero, it's game over... but your story doesn't end there. Choose from one of the following options.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0030_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10494,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Continue:
Resume the battle from where you left off, but with your own fighter at full health. Be aware that
when using this option, your battle rank will decrease.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0030_02:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10495,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Retry From Last Autosave:
End the battle and retry from an earlier point.

Return to Storyline:
End the battle and return to the Storyline.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0031_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10496,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "From the Storyline, you can experience the story of Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba.

The Storyline is divided into several chapters, and once you complete all stories in a chapter, the next chapter will be unlocked.

Once you've completed a chapter, you can go back and play it again from any point.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0033_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10497,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Memory fragments allow you to learn more about a character's past and events that unfolded behind the scenes of the main story. You can obtain them by proceeding through the story or finding them in areas you explore.

In addition to viewing them via <otherId_Icon_MemoryFragments/> on the Storyline, you can also select the Memory Fragments option from the Storyline menu or from the pause menu while exploring.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0034_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10498,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "As you progress through the story, you'll unlock special missions to defeat demons across the land.

You can accept special missions from the Storyline at any time by selecting <otherId_Icon_FreeMission/>.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0035_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10499,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "By opening the menu with <kcId_kcId_Menu_OPTIONS/> on the Storyline, you can access Rewards, Memory Fragments, Archives, Tutorials, and Options.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0037_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10500,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In the Archives you can view any battle attire, profile photos, quotes, or music tracks you have obtained.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0038_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10501,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In the Rewards menu, there are panels you can unlock to get battle attire, profile photos, and other goodies.

To unlock panels, you'll either need to meet certain conditions or spend a given number of Kimetsu Points. Kimetsu Points can be found in story areas or earned by completing various challenges.

Once you reveal the entire picture on a reward board, you'll earn a profile photo.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0039_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10502,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "While exploring, you can open the pause menu by pressing <kcId_kcId_Menu_OPTIONS/>. From there, you can access Rewards, Memory Fragments, Archives, Tutorials, and Options. You can also return to the Storyline.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0040_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10503,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "You have two maps at your disposal.

Mini-map:
The map in the upper-right corner of the screen. This provides a quick look at your surroundings.

Full Map:
Shows a general overview of the area you are exploring. View it by pressing <kcId_kcId_Field_Map/>. Your destination will be marked with a <otherId_Icon_Main01/>.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0042_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10504,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Interact with glowing spots on the field to get Kimetsu Points. These can be used to unlock reward panels. Be sure to explore every nook and cranny to collect as many as you can!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0043_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10505,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If you see a <otherId_Icon_Minievent/> on the map or while exploring an area, that indicates an available reward mission. Complete all reward missions in a named set to unlock a reward panel.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0044_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10506,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "While exploring an area as Tanjiro, you can sometimes track scents with <kcId_kcId_Field_Smell/> to reveal a path to your destination. When this option is available,
<kcId_kcId_Field_Smell/> Track Scent will appear on the left side of the screen.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0046_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10507,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "To find clues about the demon who is abducting girls, start by talking to people around town. When you hear what they have to say, a Scent of a Demon will appear in the area.

Gather intel and seek out every scent! If you don't know where to find them, track the scent with <kcId_kcId_Field_Smell/> to easily locate it.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0047_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10508,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Yushiro has hidden Tamayo's clinic with his Blood Demon Art. Along the way to the clinic will be several walls that don't actually exist, but have been created with a concealment spell.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0047_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10509,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If Yushiro's scent lingers by a wall, then you know it's a fake. Use Track Scent with <kcId_kcId_Field_Smell/> to see through the deception! Investigate a fake wall to pass through it.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0048_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10510,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Progress the story by heading to locations marked with <otherId_Icon_Main01/> or talking to characters you find there.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0049_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10511,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When a button icon lines up with the target in the center of the screen, hold down the corresponding button.

Icons always come in sets of two! Press in when the first icon aligns with the target, and release when the second one does.

If you succeed, the gauge at the top of the screen will fill. Multiple successes in a row will earn you more points.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0049_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10512,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Once the gauge is filled up to one of the gourd icons, you'll start blowing into the gourd. Mash the displayed button until the gourd breaks, then move on to the next gourd.

Your rank will be determined by your number of broken gourds and the amount of time remaining, so the faster you go, the higher your score will be!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0050_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10513,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When a button icon lines up with the target in the center of the screen, press the corresponding button. If you succeed, the gauge on the top of the screen will fill.

Multiple successes in a row will earn you more points. If your score is high enough when time runs out, you'll have succeeded in your training!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0052_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10514,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In a battle with multiple opponents, you can change which one you're actively targeting with <kcId_kcId_Battle_Target/>.

Changing targets as the tide of battle shifts is key to staying on top.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0053_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10515,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Your Slayer ID keeps a record of your online
matches. Check it to see your Battle Record.

You'll also trade IDs with your opponent after each match, so you'll be able to view their information
as well.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0053_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10516,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In the Directory, you can view the Slayer IDs
you have received.

You can store up to 300 IDs in total.
If you exceed this number, the oldest will automatically be deleted. To save your favorite IDs and prevent them from being deleted, you can choose to follow them (max 100).",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0053_02:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10517,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "By choosing "Edit Slayer ID," you can customize your Slayer ID with the profile photos and quotes you have collected. Make your very own ID and show it off to other players in online matches!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0054_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10518,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In an online match, you can fight against another player over the Internet.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0054_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10519,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Ranked Match:
Your rank points will increase or decrease depending on the outcome, which will determine your place in the rankings. Use this mode to put your skills to the test.

Custom Match:
Your rank points will not change regardless of the outcome, so you can relax and enjoy casual play. You can only match with users who have the same region and time settings as you. Use this mode when you want to play with your friends.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0054_02:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10520,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "You must decide which fighters to use and what battlefield to play on before you are matched with an opponent. Make these selections in the Choose Fighters/Battlefield menu.

By default Player 1's battlefield takes priority, but if this would result in a stage with <otherId_Icon_DAYLIGHT/> while Player 2 is using a demon character, then the match will proceed on Player 2's battlefield instead.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0055_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10521,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In Practice mode, you can learn a character's controls or combos. Utilize various settings to get the most out of your training.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0056_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10522,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "In Training mode, you can select a character to be your battle instructor.

Each character's training is divided up into ten ranks. If you can defeat your instructor within the allotted time, you will unlock the next rank. As you climb the ranks, your instructor will fight more and more fiercely.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0056_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10523,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Furthermore, each battle has tasks associated with it. If you defeat your instructor after completing a task in battle, you'll earn Kimetsu Points (one time only).

Try to complete every task!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0057_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10524,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "By spending a special bar you can Boost to enter a heightened state, increasing your attack power, along with other effects, for a limited time.

You'll return to normal when time runs out, so find the right moment to set your heart ablaze!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0058_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10525,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If you spend another special bar while Boost is active, you'll begin to Surge, granting an even larger power boost. While Surge is active, the skill gauge won't deplete!

Settle the score before time runs out and you return to your normal state.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0059_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10526,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If you touch a red mire that the Swamp Demon has placed on the ground, you'll be trapped in place. Use <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/> to break out!

Additionally, you can remove a red mire from the battlefield entirely by hitting it with a <kcId_kcId_Battle_Skill/> skill.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0059_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10527,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Watch out! Sometimes the Swamp Demon will spread a giant mire around him.

Just like the red mires, you'll be trapped if you touch it, so use <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/> to break out!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0060_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10528,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "The special gauge can be filled up to three times, and spending it will unleash a powerful Ultimate Art!

If you have filled the bar more than once, the full stock will be spent to increase the power of the resulting attack.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0061_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10529,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When you're struck by one of Yahaba's Kouketsu Arrows, you'll be knocked into the air and slammed on the ground. However, if you use a skill with <kcId_kcId_Battle_Skill/> before you land, you can get back on your feet and won't take any damage.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0062_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10530,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When Kyogai causes the room to rotate, you'll be thrown into the air and slammed onto the floor. However, if you can jump right before the the room moves you can avoid being swept up in the rotation.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0062_01:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10531,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If you fail to jump at the right time, use a skill with <kcId_kcId_Battle_Skill/> before hitting the ground to avoid taking damage.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0063_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10532,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If Enmu puts you to sleep, you won't be able to move. You'll wake up naturally after some time passes, but you can accelerate the process by rapidly using <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/>.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0064_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10533,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "If Enmu puts you to sleep, you won't be able to move. You'll wake up naturally after some time passes, but you can accelerate the process by rapidly using <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/>.

You can also wake up immediately by switching out your fighter or using an emergency escape.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0066_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10534,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "By looking at the rankings, you can check the standing of players from all over the world who have fought in ranked matches.

The list can be sorted by a variety of criteria to find the information you're most interested in.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0067_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10535,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Your overall Chapter Rank is determined by the ranks of each battle and minigame within that chapter. Improving your average will raise your Chapter Rank, so tackle every challenge to aim for the highest rank of S!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0068_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10536,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When battles with certain opponents reach their climactic moments, you'll need to time your inputs to a special animation in what's called a Final Clash.

Stay calm and be ready for anything!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0069_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10537,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Correctly completing inputs during a Final Clash will earn <otherId_Icon_Fire/>. Some challenges demand speed while others demand precise timing. The better you perform, the more <otherId_Icon_Fire/> you'll get.

Earn enough <otherId_Icon_Fire/> to fill the gauge and you'll see a special animation!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0070_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10538,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "You can play the Gourd Breaker and Tea Splasher minigames as many times as you want.

Your rank in these minigames will affect your Chapter Rank, so try to aim for the highest rank of S!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0071_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10539,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Watch out! Sometimes the Swamp Demon will spread a giant mire around him.

Just like the red mires, you'll be trapped if you touch it, so use <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/> to break out!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0072_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10540,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "You can view the memory fragments you've obtained at any time by selecting Memory Fragments from the pause menu.

They're scattered all over the map for you to discover, so keep an eye out as you explore!",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0073_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10541,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "The profile photos and quotes you attach to your Slayer ID will be displayed randomly when you play an online match.

When viewing the profile photos and quotes you've collected, a <otherId_Icon_HQ_Check/> icon will indicate that it's currently attached to your Slayer ID.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0074_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10542,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "When you quickly tilt <kcId_kcId_Battle_Move/> while simultaneously pressing <kcId_kcId_Battle_Guard/>, you will enter a parry stance.

If the opponent hits you while in this stance, you will counter their attack and stagger them. The opponent is defenseless while staggered, so use this chance to land an attack.",
  },
  "Tutorial_text_0075_00:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10543,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "You can check your reward mission progress via icons on the Storyline.

<otherId_Icon_Minievent_Clear/> means you've completed every mission.
<otherId_Icon_Minievent/> means there's still more to do.

If neither <otherId_Icon_Minievent_Clear/> nor <otherId_Icon_Minievent/> are present, then no reward missions are available.

Explore every nook and cranny and tackle them all!",
  },
  "Tutorial_BookTitle_0023:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10419,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Battle Screen",
  },
  "Tutorial_BookTitle_0027:0" => {
    "attribute": {
      "data": [
        128,
        9,
        4,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
        255,
      ],
      "type": "Buffer",
    },
    "id": 10420,
    "idSub": 0,
    "message": "Support Fighters",
